# Luminary marker — cli#511
- date: 2026-11-09
- branch: docs/publish-skill-matches-the-gate
- lead: linus-torvalds
- supporting: [michael-feathers, david-ogilvy]
- linus-torvalds (lead) — the question is what belongs to the source tree and
  what belongs to the machine. The ignore was right about the hundred skills
  the sync copies in and wrong about the one this repo wrote. The lens is what
  kept the fix to a narrow exception instead of reverting the ignore.
- michael-feathers — the skill documents a mechanism, so the mechanism is the
  source of record. Every claim in the new prose was read back against the
  script, and two of mine were wrong.
- david-ogilvy — honesty test. "It does not need the publish to have finished"
  was true when written and misleading now. The fix says which half still
  holds, rather than deleting the sentence and leaving a reader guessing.
